WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.225 --> 00:00:12.372
In the month of May, a pretty lark chose a safe spot in the green field.

2
00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:14.934
She built a nest and laid her eggs.

3
00:00:15.675 --> 00:00:19.457
In June, her eggs hatched and the chicks began to grow.

4
00:00:20.118 --> 00:00:24.621
In July, her chicks grew feathers, but they still could not fly.

5
00:00:26.162 --> 00:00:29.164
So, the mother lark had to search for food every day.

6
00:00:29.868 --> 00:00:33.389
"Feed me, feed me," her chicks chirped.

7
00:00:34.089 --> 00:00:40.351
She would fly high and low, then high and low, until she found some food.

8
00:00:42.211 --> 00:00:47.593
One day while she was out looking for food, the farmer and his son went for a walk

9
00:00:47.653 --> 00:00:48.333
in the field.

10
00:00:48.933 --> 00:00:51.954
They stopped near the lark's nest and began to talk.

11
00:00:51.974 --> 00:00:55.155
"My wheat field is ripe.

12
00:00:55.535 --> 00:00:56.555
It is harvest time.

13
00:00:57.215 --> 00:00:59.696
I must hire some men to harvest the wheat."

14
00:01:00.276 --> 00:01:01.817
The son looked disappointed.

15
00:01:02.417 --> 00:01:07.539
The mother lark saw the farmer near her nest and flew home as fast as she could.

16
00:01:07.559 --> 00:01:12.141
"Why was the farmer here?"

17
00:01:12.701 --> 00:01:13.922
the mother lark asked.

18
00:01:14.542 --> 00:01:16.823
The chicks told her what the farmer had said.

19
00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:18.784
"Should we move now?

20
00:01:19.344 --> 00:01:20.524
Where should we go?"

21
00:01:21.125 --> 00:01:22.465
one little lark asked.

22
00:01:22.485 --> 00:01:28.628
"We do not need to worry," the mother lark replied.

23
00:01:29.308 --> 00:01:31.009
"We do not need to move.

24
00:01:31.649 --> 00:01:34.210
The farmer is not ready to harvest yet."

25
00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:39.091
The mother lark went out for food again the next day.

26
00:01:39.751 --> 00:01:43.572
She flew left, then right, then left, then right.

27
00:01:44.212 --> 00:01:49.534
While she was zigzagging over the field, the farmer was talking to his son below.

28
00:01:49.554 --> 00:01:54.255
"My wheat field is ripe," he said.

29
00:01:54.275 --> 00:01:55.756
"It is harvest time.

30
00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:59.698
I must ask my friends to help me harvest my wheat."

31
00:02:00.298 --> 00:02:02.900
The son agreed, but he still looked disappointed.

32
00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:08.523
The mother lark saw the farmer near her nest and flew home as fast as she could.

33
00:02:12.826 --> 00:02:14.026
was the farmer here?"

34
00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:15.747
the mother lark asked.

35
00:02:16.368 --> 00:02:18.649
The chicks told her what the farmer had said.

36
00:02:18.669 --> 00:02:20.610
"Should we move now?

37
00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:22.271
Where should we go?"

38
00:02:22.871 --> 00:02:23.412
one asked.

39
00:02:26.556 --> 00:02:29.977
"We do not need to worry," the mother lark replied.

40
00:02:29.997 --> 00:02:32.278
"We do not need to move.

41
00:02:32.858 --> 00:02:35.359
The farmer is not ready to harvest yet."

42
00:02:36.739 --> 00:02:40.200
The mother lark continued to search for food every day.

43
00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:44.081
Whenever she flew low, she looked at the wheat closely.

44
00:02:44.681 --> 00:02:47.742
She noticed the grain was ripe and falling off the stalk.

45
00:02:49.983 --> 00:02:51.683
The farmer noticed the wheat too.

46
00:02:52.303 --> 00:02:54.644
He and his son took a walk in the field.

47
00:02:55.264 --> 00:02:58.866
The farmer said to his son, "My wheat field is ripe.

48
00:02:59.226 --> 00:03:00.246
It is harvest time.

49
00:03:00.866 --> 00:03:02.927
You and I must harvest the wheat."

50
00:03:03.548 --> 00:03:05.969
The son did not look disappointed anymore.

51
00:03:06.569 --> 00:03:08.610
He had a big smile on his face.

52
00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:12.652
"Why was the farmer here?"

53
00:03:13.192 --> 00:03:14.352
the mother lark asked.

54
00:03:14.933 --> 00:03:17.133
The chicks told her what the farmer had said.

55
00:03:17.153 --> 00:03:19.074
"Should we move now?

56
00:03:19.615 --> 00:03:20.695
Where should we go?"

57
00:03:21.255 --> 00:03:22.376
one little lark asked.

58
00:03:26.484 --> 00:03:29.965
"Yes, it is time to move," the mother lark replied.

59
00:03:29.985 --> 00:03:33.486
"We will build a new nest away from the fields.

60
00:03:34.086 --> 00:03:35.927
The farmer is ready to harvest."

61
00:03:35.947 --> 00:03:38.247
"How do you know?"

62
00:03:38.748 --> 00:03:40.128
another little lark asked.

63
00:03:40.148 --> 00:03:44.869
"A farmer is ready to harvest when he is ready to do it himself."
